  "body": "## What changed\n\nPhase 1 of #763: **`OpFrame`** — the one machining-frame seam in\n`crates/app/src/operation/frame.rs` — composes the two existing frame\nmechanisms (the setup's `part_alignment` from #326 and the op's 3+2\n`Tilt` from M5.1 B) behind one door, and `collect_job` reads through it:\n\n- `OpFrame::of(op)` built once per generation; material and heights\n  resolve through it; the tilt frame comes from\n  `OpFrame::checked_frame` — one construction site, the refusal keeping\n  its exact words and its exact precedence (after the heights resolve,\n  the job's error-order law).\n- The contract is stated once in the module header: D / S / L frames,\n  right-to-left composition `p_L = T(A(p_D))`, the CL wrapping back via\n  `TiltedFrame::world_path` (identity clone without a tilt), and the\n  furniture law (stock / WCS / fixtures live in S: never aligned, but\n  read local by the tilt).\n- Heights and bounds in L ship correct from day one\n  (`aabb_local_of`, `height_z_local`): they resolve against FULLY\n  TRANSFORMED geometry, never a `z − origin.z` shift of the S box —\n  the shift is only correct while the tool axis is the world Z.\n\n**No refusal lifted, no post change, no generator change.** The four\nverified kinds, picks, area controls and tilt-in-aligned-setups keep\ntheir refusals; the later phases lift them one by one, each with its\nnumeric pin.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `crates/app/tests/opframe_seam.rs` (8 tests) + the seam's inline\n  unit tests (6): identity passthrough; zero-tilt index reproduces the\n  prismatic path EXACTLY move-for-move (the identity-bits law); a\n  tilted face runs in its own plane (every endpoint maps back into the\n  L1-folded height band over the local silhouette, tool axis =\n  hand-computed Rx(45)); 90-degree alignment turns the solid and its\n  TopOfModel height (15, not 10); 180-degree alignment mirrors the\n  facets by hand math; alignment × tilt composition pinned against\n  hand-composed transforms; local heights/boxes read fully transformed\n  geometry (and provably NOT the z-shift); picks stay refused by name\n  while the door Phase 2 will read through is already aligned.\n- Capability gates: unchanged by design; the tilted-move refusal keeps\n  its existing verbatim pin in `tests/inverted_post.rs`.\n- The four kinds' aligned generation keeps its pins in the #326 suites\n  (`plane_align`, `axis_align`, `rest_across_setups`, …), run by the\n  same gate.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The L-frame height/AABB resolve methods are pinned by tests only —\n  no production call site switches onto them until Phase 2+ lifts the\n  matching refusals (deliberate: the seam lands behavior-identical).\n- The boundary/region builders (`boundary_ctx`, `material_region`,\n  `boundary_picks`) still build their own frames from `op.params.tilt()`\n  — they move onto the seam in the later phases.\n\nChangelog: feat: one machining-frame seam (OpFrame) composing part_alignment and TiltedFrame behind a single door; generation reads through it byte-identically (#763, PR)\n\nRefs #763\n",
